{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 3"},"body":"The full Gaussian statement, including the construction clause, identifies the atomic-certificate paper.\n\nInspected: Read full challenge, Gaussian/dual lattice definitions, construction blocks and tail predicate; compared atomic thm:gaussian, energy headline and older universal-optimality headline.\n\nCapture rebinding by Codex, 26 October 2026: the Atlas capture revision changed after an outside-report wording correction. The pinned Lean text, configuration, paper text and proposed relation are unchanged; no new review is implied.","content_sha256":"sha256:1e1693bff6cf8a4d461c02452a25e9dcc005bdd96ec03e35b97f73d97cbf7141","fingerprint":"sha256:c2f342c5171873715e31a732e1d5fa4a14b0bf63b6243f49640d3ea96fade57d","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The full Gaussian statement, including the construction clause, identifies the atomic-certificate paper.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:8654d0128126080c26a7e97bb8993fd934f9635d9373f6a0a69d3eb1fd857d4e","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.AtomicTriangular.sharp_gaussian_minorants_with_construction"],"explanation":"The theorem produces a radial real Schwartz minorant for every positive Gaussian parameter, a nonnegative real Fourier transform, equality at nonzero triangular-lattice points and zeros at nonzero dual points. The final conditional AtomicConstruction expands the alpha>=1 construction into two 20-by-20 interpolation blocks and a summable tail, matching the atomic Gaussian theorem rather than universal energy minimality.","fingerprint":"sha256:b0e6154e4b8eaf18ca27032ef6e22e57476c6093123ba91ace96a52b5c2655d1","limitations":"The explicit coefficient/error-bound encoding was inspected but not independently verified against the full construction proof; this is a source correspondence, not a proof replay.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"An-atomic-certificate-for-triangular-lattice-universal-optimality-September-26-2026#thm:gaussian","statement_sha256":"sha256:f35a3d68a7e91c7acbd80bc82c33b9e514c171527a19bd59d7fcf2c786c1b917"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/TriangularGaussian.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-atomic-certificate-for-triangular-lattice-universal-optimality-September-26-2026/build/main.tex#L95"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:TriangularGaussian","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/518bc0c1a9068479a60c1a7c.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/518bc0c1a9068479a60c1a7c.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/518bc0c1a9068479a60c1a7c.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/518bc0c1a9068479a60c1a7c.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/518bc0c1a9068479a60c1a7c.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.AtomicTriangular.sharp_gaussian_minorants_with_construction","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/TriangularGaussian.lean","line":263,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"8654d0128126080c26a7e97bb8993fd934f963